{"parentUuid": null, "isSidechain": true, "promptId": "3082e11a-e882-451c-8133-3b8ab114d562", "agentId": "addef9c7406ffa00a", "type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "You need to fix three code quality issues in `tests/conftest.py` in the repo at `/Users/test/Projects/studyengine/.worktrees/background-jobs`. These are the Postgres test fixtures that were just added.\n\n## Fix 1 (Critical): Engine leak on Alembic failure in pg_engine\n\nCurrent code in `pg_engine`:\n```python\nengine = _ce(_TEST_PG_URL)\nalembic_cfg = AlembicConfig(\"alembic.ini\")\nalembic_cfg.set_main_option(\"sqlalchemy.url\", _TEST_PG_URL)\nalembic_command.upgrade(alembic_cfg, \"head\")\nyield engine\nengine.dispose()\n```\n\nIf `alembic_command.upgrade()` raises, the engine is never disposed. Fix with try/finally:\n```python\nengine = _ce(_TEST_PG_URL)\ntry:\n    alembic_cfg = AlembicConfig(\"alembic.ini\")\n    alembic_cfg.set_main_option(\"sqlalchemy.url\", _TEST_PG_URL)\n    alembic_command.upgrade(alembic_cfg, \"head\")\nexcept Exception:\n    engine.dispose()\n    raise\nyield engine\nengine.dispose()\n```\n\n## Fix 2 (Important): Session leak in pg_authed_client\n\nCurrent code creates a session without try/finally:\n```python\nsession = Session()\nuser = User(...)\nsession.add(user)\nsession.commit()\ntoken = uuid.uuid4().hex\nuser_session = UserSession(...)\nsession.add(user_session)\nsession.commit()\nsession.close()\n```\n\nIf the second `commit()` raises, `session.close()` is never called. Fix:\n```python\nsession = Session()\ntry:\n    user = User(email=\"test@example.com\", display_name=\"Test User\")\n    session.add(user)\n    session.commit()\n    token = uuid.uuid4().hex\n    user_session = UserSession(\n        token=token,\n        user_id=user.id,\n        expires_at=datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(days=30),\n    )\n    session.add(user_session)\n    session.commit()\nfinally:\n    session.close()\n```\n\n## Fix 3 (Minor): Remove deferred import aliases in pg_engine and pg_override_db\n\nThe imports `from sqlalchemy import create_engine as _ce`, `from sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker as _sm`, and `from sqlalchemy import text as _text` are deferred inside the fixture functions with aliases. The project already imports `create_engine`, `sessionmaker`, and `text` at the top of conftest.py. Remove the deferred imports and use the already-imported names directly.\n\nAlso remove the deferred `from alembic.config import Config as AlembicConfig` and `from alembic import command as alembic_command` \u2014 add those to the top-level imports at the top of conftest.py if they're not already there.\n\n## After fixing\n\nRun:\n```bash\ncd /Users/test/Projects/studyengine/.worktrees/background-jobs\npython -m pytest tests/ -x -q --ignore=tests/test_pg_smoke.py 2>&1 | tail -5\n```\n\nExpected: all 371 SQLite tests still pass.\n\nThen commit:\n```bash\ngit add tests/conftest.py\ngit commit -m \"fix: resource cleanup in Postgres test fixtures\"\n```\n\nReport STATUS: DONE when committed.\n"}, "uuid": "688b455b-125d-47aa-8314-3bdfe0bff2c8", "timestamp": "2026-04-23T01:36:15.995Z", "userType": "external", "entrypoint": "cli", "cwd": "/Users/test/Projects/studyengine/.worktrees/background-jobs", "sessionId": "3f5802ab-0587-4c78-8a7e-80ca419e724f", "version": "2.1.117", "gitBranch": "test-branch", "slug": "hazy-honking-kernighan"}
